Subject: [PATCH] sun300iw1p1: preserve FEL payloads in simpleboot

FES has already initialized the 64 MiB DRAM before the host uploads
Linux, OpenSBI, DTB and initrd. Repeating init_DRAM in simpleboot runs
the destructive DRAM write test, overwriting the kernel at 0x80000000.
Skip DRAM initialization only for the FEL falcon wrapper. Falcon2
still initializes DRAM before loading its flash bundle.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/board/sun300iw1p1/simpleboot/simpleboot_falcon.mk b/board/sun300iw1p1/simpleboot/simpleboot_falcon.mk
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/sun300iw1p1/simpleboot/simpleboot_falcon.mk
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+# FEL uploads payloads after FES initializes the board's 64 MiB DRAM.
+CFG_FALCON_FEL_DRAM_SIZE=64
diff --git a/simpleboot/main/simpleboot_main.c b/simpleboot/main/simpleboot_main.c
--- a/simpleboot/main/simpleboot_main.c
+++ b/simpleboot/main/simpleboot_main.c
@@ -93,7 +93,10 @@ void main(void)
 		goto _BOOT_ERROR;
 	record_time("board_init");
 
-#ifdef FPGA_PLATFORM
+#ifdef CFG_FALCON_FEL_DRAM_SIZE
+	/* FES initialized DRAM; reinitialization would destroy FEL payloads. */
+	dram_size = CFG_FALCON_FEL_DRAM_SIZE;
+#elif defined(FPGA_PLATFORM)
 	dram_size = sunxi_fpga_dram_init((void *)sunxi_bootparam_get_dram_buf());
 #else
 	dram_size = init_DRAM(0, (void *)sunxi_bootparam_get_dram_buf());
